RequestObjectTag policies ignored for PutObjectTagging
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/security/findings/671c398339708191afd6e9c8dd91c388?repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin&sev=low
Criticality: low (attack path: low)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Valid issue. Fixed in commit `1b89dda` (`Honor request tag conditions for object tagging`).

We first added AWS-backed `s3-tests` coverage for the real API surface:
- `test_bucket_policy_put_obj_tagging_request_object_tag`
- `test_bucket_policy_put_obj_version_tagging_request_object_tag`

Those tests passed against AWS and failed locally before the fix, confirming
that both `PutObjectTagging` and `PutObjectVersionTagging` must honor
`s3:RequestObjectTag/...` bucket-policy conditions.

The fix in `1b89dda` threaded request-tag XML through the actual object-tagging
authorization path, so `lock_object_for_authorized_tagging` now evaluates
bucket policy with request tags for tagging writes instead of only existing
object tags. The change also added matching `server-core` regressions for both
current-object and versioned tagging.

