# Summary
Introduced: RequestObjectTag condition evaluation is wired only for PutObject-related flows, leaving PutObjectTagging/PutObjectVersionTagging policy checks unaware of request tags.
The commit adds RequestObjectTag condition support in the policy engine, but PutObjectTagging authorization still calls bucket_policy_decision_for_object, which only injects ExistingObjectTag values into PolicyRequest. As a result, RequestObjectTag conditions are evaluated against empty request tags for tagging operations. An authenticated client with tagging permission can set arbitrary tags even when a bucket policy is intended to restrict tag values, potentially enabling escalation via ExistingObjectTag-based access rules.

