## Rubric
- [x] Locate PutObjectTagging authorization path and confirm it uses bucket_policy_decision_for_object.
- [x] Verify bucket_policy_decision_for_object only injects ExistingObjectTag values and never request tags.
- [x] Confirm RequestObjectTag condition evaluation relies on request_object_tag_value and missing tags return NoMatch.
- [x] Trace fallback to requester_can_manage_object_tags for NoMatch, allowing bucket/object owners.
- [ ] Build/run PoC test to demonstrate denial bypass (blocked by missing libisal dependency).
## Report
Attempted dynamic reproduction by adding a unit test (patch in artifacts) and running `cargo test -p server-core put_object_tagging_request_object_tag_condition_not_applied -- --nocapture`, but the build failed because `libisal` is missing (ec-sys build.rs error: “libisal not found; install intel-isa-l or set PKG_CONFIG_PATH”). Valgrind and gdb are not installed (commands returned 127). Code inspection shows PutObjectTagging authorization flows through `lock_object_for_authorized_tagging` → `requester_can_manage_object_tags_with_bucket_policy` → `bucket_policy_decision_for_object` (crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs:4159-4189, 3584-3605). `bucket_policy_decision_for_object` only injects existing object tags and never populates request tags (coordinator.rs:3432-3460), while PutObject-like paths use `bucket_policy_decision_for_put_object_action` which does populate request tags via `with_request_object_tags` (coordinator.rs:3494-3514; crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs:263-265). `PolicyRequest::new` initializes `request_object_tags` to empty (bucket_policy.rs:163-180), and RequestObjectTag conditions read `request_object_tag_value` (bucket_policy.rs:969-977, 332-336); for `StringEquals`, missing tags yield `NoMatch` (bucket_policy.rs:1034-1042). As a result, RequestObjectTag conditions do not match PutObjectTagging requests, leading to `PolicyEvaluation::NoMatch` and fallback to `requester_can_manage_object_tags` (coordinator.rs:3584-3605), which allows bucket/object owners (coordinator.rs:3258-3269), enabling tag restriction bypass.

